+   entry from JS_LAYOUT_RT_GC_FRAME's top, if there is room below its
+   end, and popped on exit), each a word { uint32_t size, live } then the
+   object's cell; an async function's in its frame's cell (each a word
+   then the object, its header JS_LAYOUT_GC_EMBEDDED_WORD's with its
+   frame's GC bits, and the distance back to the frame cell's header as
+   its reference count). JS_GCFramePin: the frame objects made so far may
+   be held past their frames (given to code that may keep them): they
+   stay, and their slots are not reused (native code makes objects only
+   in the slots above the floor, and pops no lower). JS_MarkEmbeddedObjects:
+   for the mark function of the cell `owner` that holds such objects in
+   [start, end): marks their children, and gives them its GC bits. */
+JS_EXTERN void JS_GCFramePin(JSRuntime *rt);
